{"id":"f7166ba0-7ec5-498e-9a38-5e03844fec30","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"a4eb2d27eddc588a","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/preview-session.ts","baseline":{"blob":"a6eaf5c1e0b087058b359b7659e1d4f14ade94fb","start":0,"end":46},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","Hub","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/hub","\""]},"context":{"after":"2c1cb6475bc215a0"}},"payload":{"text":"A dev server, in Run and Debug (RUNNING.md, *The model*): as it comes up it's a session there, with Restart and Stop on the debug toolbar (a session on its own has no row in Call Stack), what it says going\nto the Debug Console as well as its terminal. It's a window onto the service, not a way of running it: the server's the terminal's\n(workbench/runs.ts), stopping the session stops it, and however it ends, the session does. It claims nothing a debugging session\nwould: no status bar, and Run and Debug isn't brought forward. Nothing here steps: it has no threads, and the toolbar has Restart\nand Stop. What its pages' recorded stops (a breakpoint in their code) record, it tells the Margin (recorded-stops.ts).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T17:59:09.938Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T17:59:09.938Z"}
